# Telegram Mini App — Production Development & Deployment Plan

## Overview

Build a production-ready **Telegram Web App (Mini App)** as a **standalone Next.js project** (separate repo/folder from the existing Laravel backend, since Prisma is the data layer). The app runs inside Telegram's WebView across iOS, Android, Desktop, and Web clients.

### Objectives

- Secure, server-side validation of Telegram `initData` (HMAC-SHA256, replay protection, timing-safe comparison).
- Automatic adaptation to Telegram theme variables (light/dark/custom) via a CSS-variable bridge into shadcn/ui tokens.
- Dual-language support: English (LTR) and Arabic (RTL) with locale-segmented routing and `dir` switching.
- Production hardening: structured logging, error boundaries, rate limiting, CSP, pooled DB connections, CI/CD.

### Locked Tech Stack

| Concern | Choice |
|---|---|
| Framework | Next.js 15 (App Router, TypeScript, RSC) |
| ORM / DB | Prisma 6 + PostgreSQL (Neon/Supabase/RDS; pooled for serverless) |
| UI | Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui (CSS-variable theming, logical properties for RTL) |
| Telegram SDK | Official `telegram-web-app.js` script + `@telegram-apps/sdk-react` types |
| i18n | `next-intl` (locales: `en` default, `ar`; `localePrefix: "as-needed"`) |
| Client state | Zustand (UI state) + TanStack Query v5 (server state) |
| Validation | Zod (shared API/form schemas) |
| Auth | `jose` JWT in `httpOnly; secure; sameSite=none` cookie, minted only after initData validation |
| Logging | pino (server, structured JSON) + React error boundaries (client) |

