### Task 7 — Error Handling, Logging & Hardening

1. Add `src/app/[locale]/error.tsx` (route-level, localized retry UI) and `src/app/global-error.tsx` (root fallback with own `<html>`).
2. Pino logging conventions: request-scoped child loggers with route + userId; never log `initData`, tokens, or cookie values.
3. Security headers in `next.config.ts`:

```ts
headers: async () => [{
  source: "/(.*)",
  headers: [
    { key: "Content-Security-Policy",
      value: "frame-ancestors https://web.telegram.org https://*.telegram.org;" },
    { key: "X-Content-Type-Options", value: "nosniff" },
    { key: "Referrer-Policy", value: "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" },
  ],
}]
```

   ⚠️ Never set `X-Frame-Options: DENY` — Telegram Web embeds the app in an iframe.
4. Zod-validate every API route body/query; reject oversized payloads.
5. Optional: Sentry (`@sentry/nextjs`) for client + server error capture.

**Acceptance:** Thrown errors render localized boundaries (no white screen); headers verified via `curl -I`; no sensitive values in logs.

